     "literals": [],
     "text": "The budget book prints collaborative tuition twice: **$782,867** for the tuition, and a **Circuit Breaker** line of **−$480,204** beneath it. Town Meeting votes the difference, **$302,663**. So the line is voted on the assumption that the state’s reimbursement will pay part of the bills."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [],
     "text": "The reimbursement does not arrive in the line. It sits in its own fund, and pays a bill only when a bill is charged to that fund. Until then the school budget pays, and the line shows as over budget. A charge to the fund afterwards lowers what the school budget spent, so it raises what was left."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [],
     "text": "What the school budget leaves unspent returns to the town as free cash. What the circuit breaker fund leaves stays in the fund, to be spent within a year of arriving (DESE)."
    }
   ],
