     "literals": [
      "31 December 2025"
     ],
     "text": "**Shows.** The circuit breaker paid tuition bills as they came in FY2023, FY2024 and FY2025. In FY2026 it paid $4,005 before June, while the state’s $325,970 for the year was in the fund by 31 December 2025. The IDEA grant paid $287,108 toward private tuition that year, by our match on the payee."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [
      "29 June"
     ],
     "text": "**Does not show.** Why the fund was left untouched until 29 June: a late claim, a choice to keep the money for later, or an ordinary year-end clean-up all fit the same postings. Nothing held says which."
    },
    {
     "figures": {},
     "literals": [],
     "text": "**Would settle it.** The district’s year-end close memo for the school budget, and the circuit breaker claim with the state’s payment schedule. Both are on What we cannot answer."
    }
